// LANGUAGE TEMPLATE — copy this file to src/js/locales/<code>.js and
// translate every value.
//
// How to use this file:
//   1. Copy it:  cp src/js/locales/language.js.template src/js/locales/<code>.js
//      <code> is the language's two-letter ISO 639-1 code (fr, de, ko, …).
//   2. Every value below is the English source string, wrapped in TR(...).
//      Replace the argument with your translation and leave TR itself alone —
//      it's a no-op at runtime, present only so this file works if it's
//      accidentally imported before you've translated it, and so a `grep -n
//      "TR("` shows every line you still have left.
//   3. Leave every key ('nav.tab.logbook', 'lb.save', …) exactly as it is.
//      Keys are how the app looks phrases up — renaming or removing one
//      breaks the app for that language.
//   4. Entries written as `({ n }) => TR(...)` or `({ name }) => TR(...)` are
//      functions, not plain strings, because the English phrase bends around
//      a number or a name ("3 people" / "Restore Docs LogBook"). Keep the
//      `({ ... }) =>` part unchanged and translate only inside TR(). Rework
//      the sentence around the variable however your language needs to —
//      English pluralizes with -s; your language may not need to mark plural
//      at all, or may need a different word depending on the count. There is
//      no plural-rule system to fight here: write the sentence the way it
//      would actually read.
//   5. `[TABLE]`, `[NOTE]`, `[TIP]`, `[IMPORTANT]`, `[WARNING]`, `[CAUTION]`
//      inside 'guide.md' are Markdown/app syntax, not English words — leave
//      the markers themselves alone and translate only the surrounding
//      prose. See src/js/locales/ja.js for a worked example of the whole
//      file, including this one.
//   6. When every TR(...) is gone, register the language in src/js/i18n.js:
//        - import your file and add it to CATALOGS
//        - add a row to LOCALES: { code, label (the language's own name,
//          e.g. 'Français'), short, tag (BCP-47, e.g. 'fr'), manifest }
//        - copy src/manifest.ja.webmanifest to manifest.<code>.webmanifest,
//          translate name/description/shortcuts, and register it in
//          scripts/copy-static.js
//   7. A key you never get to is not a crash — i18n.js falls back to the
//      English string for anything missing, so a partial translation ships
//      safely. Run `grep -c "TR(" src/js/locales/<code>.js` to see how many
//      are left.
//
// A no-op: TR('x') === 'x'. It exists purely as a grep target — see step 2.
